<section class="section-padding bg-light-subtle">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:900px">
        <span class="section-kicker">Your information</span>
        <h1 class="display-6 mb-3">ManGROOVES privacy notice</h1>
        <p class="lead">ManGROOVES collects only the information needed to coordinate community mangrove monitoring, verify field evidence, and support conservation decisions.</p>

        <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm"><div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
            <h2 class="h4">Information collected</h2>
            <p>Guardian accounts contain a name, email address, optional phone number, assigned barangay, consent time, and security activity. Reports contain precise coordinates, location accuracy when GPS is used, photos, checklist answers, species traits, counts, remarks, and follow-up links. Expert decisions, feedback, badges, notifications, and audit events are also retained.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Why it is used</h2>
            <p>The information is used to authenticate users, validate and review reports, group verified observations into monitoring sites, track health and survival over time, contact or coach guardians, recognize verified contributions, produce conservation analytics, secure the service, and maintain an accountable record of official actions.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Who can see it</h2>
            <p>Guardians can see their own complete reports. Guardians in the same barangay may see shared cluster-level health, species, counts, and dates, but another guardian's photo, precise report coordinates, report reference, and private expert feedback are hidden. Authorized experts and system administrators can inspect report evidence for verification and operations. Public visitors do not receive account or report records.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Retention and protection</h2>
            <p>Records are retained while needed for monitoring history, legal accountability, and approved conservation programs. Administrators should publish a local retention schedule before production use. The application uses role checks, password hashing, CSRF protection, session expiry and revocation, audit logging, validated uploads, and access-controlled report views. No internet service can promise absolute security.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Your choices and rights</h2>
            <p>You may review and correct profile data in Settings. Requests to access, correct, restrict, or delete information that cannot be changed in the app should be sent to the operating CCENRO office. Some verified environmental and audit records may need to be preserved, in which case the account can be suspended and identifying access limited instead of deleting the monitoring history.</p>

            <h2 class="h4 mt-4">Contact and local publication</h2>
            <p class="mb-0">For the pilot, contact the Cebu City Environment and Natural Resources Office through Cebu City's official contact channels. Before public deployment, the operating organization must add its named privacy officer, current contact details, retention periods, lawful basis, and incident-response channel to this notice in accordance with the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 and its own approved policy.</p>
        </div></div>
    </div>
</section>
